 "_comment": "Which module owns each table (PR-DB-2.1). A module owns a table when its own app/models.py declares it; the tables the shared library declares for every module (smo_shared) are under `shared`. tests_integration/test_table_owners.py fails when a table is missing here, listed twice, or listed under a module that does not declare it; scripts/check_migration_matches_models.py fails when the migrated Postgres has a table that is not here. Add a table here in the same change that adds it. `_retired` lists tables whose module was removed (A1 Related, October 2026: out of scope): nothing reads or writes them, they stay in the database until a later revision drops them (expand, then contract: the release that removed the code cannot drop what the previous release still uses).",
